===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[make]] a [[mistake]], especially when it is [[careless]] or [[stupid]].
#: {{ux|en|to '''blunder''' in preparing a medical prescription}}
## {{lb|en|chess|intransitive}} To make a very bad move.
## {{lb|en|chess|transitive}} To make a very bad move and thereby cause the loss of (a piece).
# {{lb|en|intransitive|with adverb or preposition}} To [[move]] in an [[unsteady]] way.
#* '''October 6, 1759''', {{w|Oliver Goldsmith}}, ''The Bee'' No. 1
#*: I was never distinguished for address, and have often even '''blundered''' in making my bow.
#* {{RQ:Dryden Fables|chapter=Palamon and Arcite|passage='''blunders''' on, and staggers every pace}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|with adverb or preposition}} To [[enter]] a place or become [[involved]] in a [[difficult]] situation by mistake.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1714|author=w:Humphry Ditton|title=A discourse concerning the resurrection of Jesus Christ
|passage=To '''blunder''' an adversary.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|archaic}} To [[do]] or [[treat]] in a [[blundering]] manner; to [[confuse]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1676|author=w:Edward Stillingfleet|title=A Defence of the Discourse Concerning the Idolatry Practised in the Church of Rome
|passage=He '''blunders''' and confounds all these together.}}

